.TH "RECORD\-GET\-FOLKSONOMY\-TABLE\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-get\-folksonomy\-table\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-get\-folksonomy\-table\.sh\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-get\-folksonomy\-table\.sh\fR extracts the list of tag variable names from the folksonomy library at \fBexample/lib\.folksonomy\.sh\fR\. It finds all lines invoking \fBrecord_make_tag\fR, strips everything from the \fB=\fR sign onwards, and prints the resulting variable names to standard output \(em one per line\.
.P
The path to \fBexample/lib\.folksonomy\.sh\fR is hard\-coded; the script must be run from the root of the RECORD project directory\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success, or if no matches are found\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if \fBexample/lib\.folksonomy\.sh\fR does not exist or cannot be read\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
List all folksonomy tag variable names:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-get\-folksonomy\-table\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Use the output to drive further processing:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-get\-folksonomy\-table\.sh | while read tag; do
    echo "Processing $tag"
done
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
