.SH "BUGS"
The path \fBexample/lib\.folksonomy\.sh\fR is hard\-coded, so the script will silently produce no output or fail with a \fBgrep\fR error if run from any directory other than the RECORD project root\.
.P
The script accepts no \fB\-\-help\fR or \fB\-\-version\fR flags, unlike other RECORD utilities\.
.P
If \fBgrep\fR finds no matches it exits with status 1, which will propagate as a non\-zero exit from the script and may be misinterpreted as an error by calling scripts using \fBset \-e\fR\.
